Section 6 (Minn. Stat. 97B.031, subd. 1): A person may take big game and wolves with a firearm only if:
Section 6 (Minn. Stat. 97B.031, subd. 1): (1) any rifle, shotgun, or handgun used is a caliber of at least .22 inches and has centerfire ignition;
Section 6 (Minn. Stat. 97B.031, subd. 1): (2) the firearm is loaded only with single projectile ammunition;
Section 6 (Minn. Stat. 97B.031, subd. 1): (4) any muzzleloader used has the projectile loaded only at the muzzle;
Section 7 (Minn. Stat. 97B.031, subd. 7): During the regular firearms deer season, all legal firearms may be used statewide.
Section 3 (Minn. Stat. 97A.015, subd. 51): (3) for an electronic ignition system, the battery is removed and is disconnected from the firearm; and
Section 3 (Minn. Stat. 97A.015, subd. 51): (4) for an encapsulated powder charge ignition system, the primer and powder charge are removed from the firearm.
